1. CORE DESIGN PRINCIPLE
   ==================================================

The vehicle must NOT think primarily in terms of lanes.

This is the central SIH requirement.

The planning question is:

“What region of the currently observed road is safely traversable, and what trajectory gets the vehicle toward its goal while respecting dynamic obstacles, road boundaries, vehicle dynamics and uncertainty?”

Therefore:

CAMERA:
semantic understanding / object classes / drivable-space cues

LiDAR:
3D geometry / obstacle position / range / free-space geometry

RADAR:
range / relative velocity / robust motion information

FUSION:
combine complementary observations into persistent world-model tracks

PREDICTION:
estimate where dynamic agents may move next

RISK:
estimate collision/TTC/clearance

BEHAVIOR:
decide CRUISE / FOLLOW / CAUTION / AVOID / EMERGENCY_BRAKE / STOP

PLANNER:
generate and score multiple collision-free trajectories

CONTROL:
track the selected trajectory

VEHICLE DYNAMICS:
determine actual resulting motion

Then repeat.

